|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| Main Title             | (utitl1(n))                                         |
|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|EQ6 input file name= swxrcaft.6i                                              |
|Description= "React a Ca/Na ion exchanger with flowing seawater"              |
|Version level= 8.0                                                            |
|Revised 08/04/97    Revisor= T.J. Wolery                                      |
|This is part of the EQ3/6 Test Case Library                                   |
|                                                                              |
|  React a Ca/Na ion exchanger with seawater in a fluid-centered               |
|flow-through open system. The exchanger composition in equilibrium with the   |
|fresh seawater is nearly saturated with Na. The reactant exchanger is         |
|nearly saturated with Ca.                                                     |
|                                                                              |
|  Purpose: to test the generic ion exchange modeling capability in the case   |
|of an exchanger reactant.                                                     |
|                                                                              |
|  This problem has no actual redox aspect. The oxygen fugacity was set to     |
|the atmospheric value in the initializing EQ3NR run, and O2(aq) and H2(aq)    |
|are present on the data file used (com), so this provides redox poising.      |
|Do not set iopt(15) to 1 to suppress all redox.                               |
|                                                                              |
|                                                                              |
|                            References                                        |
|                                                                              |
|None                                                                          |
|                                                                              |
|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
